            <div xml:id="d506">

                <pb facs="0860" n="813" xml:id="pg813"/>

                <head>506. Telegram 1695 to Geneva<anchor n="1" xml:id="d506-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1956-02-29">February 29,
                        1956</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <pb facs="d506-1" n="1" type="facsimile" xml:id="d506-1"/>
                <p>1695. For Johnson.</p>
                <p>Communists returned to UNCMAC February 25 list of 2720 missing UNC personnel
                    handed them by UNCMAC November 26. Notation in Korean after each name indicates
                    individual disposition. Notations presently being translated and UNCMAC expects
                    transmit Washington with comments and analysis March 3.</p>
                <p>FYI Message from CINCUNC indicates 1084 still carried on list as “no data
                    available”. We are not repeat not sanguine that any useful new information
                    provided, although can not be certain until translation completed. End FYI</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#bold">Dulles</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
